  "schema_findings": {
    "new_field": "Exactly hse_supported: bool immediately after hsi_supported in existing PllLimits/PeripheralPllLimits; one identical comment admits oscillator and bypass functional references with rate bounds only. No duty field, certificate, separate mode branch, width change or new record.",
    "required_behavior": "For a present PLL object, hse_supported is required and nonnullable in both Deserialize input models. No field/struct default, alias, custom deserializer or Option was added. true and false are representable; semantic family qualification belongs to validation. Omitted field, null and nonboolean JSON values are rejected by the ordinary derived bool contract. Static conclusion; no new serialization probe was run.",
    "serialization": "cw32-data-serde derives Serialize and Deserialize through record!, with no skip rule on either support bool: false remains explicit and the new field follows hsi_supported in declaration/derived serialization order. Generator input derives Deserialize only. Static template has no serialization derives and requires the new bool in struct construction.",
    "outer_option": "Unchanged pll:Option in both owned input models with #[serde(default)]. Missing or null pll remains None; project serde still omits None on serialization. Static metadata retains Option<PeripheralPllLimits>. No unqualified family gains a PLL record.",
    "unknown_fields": "PLL records do not deny unknown fields; unchanged. New readers reject old present-PLL objects lacking the required bool. Older permissive readers may ignore the added key; this does not prove qualification or compatibility of new behavior.",
    "old_fields": "All 12 old PLL field names, relative order, widths and representations are unchanged. Input/output bins remain four/five tuple arrays in owned models and static references in generated metadata. Exact insertion reversal preserves every other byte in all three complete model files, including native LSE.",
    "api_compatibility": "Public Rust struct literals and exhaustive destructuring require coordinated adjustment. Derived Serialize/Debug/Hash contents change. No source, ABI, binary or serialized-byte compatibility is claimed.",
    "functional_meaning": "A family qualification fact for the approved documented crystal/bypass composition, not a numeric internal-duty certificate, new pulse guarantee, board certification or post-loss recovery guarantee."
  },
